      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χMT at 300 K is 56.52 cm3 K mol−1 (theory 56.68 for four Dy3+), decreasing to 31.40 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. AC susceptibility under 0 dc field (3 Oe ac, 111–2311 Hz) shows in-phase and out-of-phase signals, frequency dependence, and Cole–Cole plots (α = 0.32–0.68 at 3–10 K) indicating SMM-type slow relaxation with a wide distribution of relaxation times and a possible additional process below 5 K. Combined Direct/Raman/Orbach fit of ln τ vs T−1 (3–10 K) gives Ueff = 45.7 K and τ0 = 1.23×10−7 s.",
        "measurements": [
